Akaunting core parity report (report)
Baseline: akaunting/akaunting@edde6b54f27ee0635b9a5dbde52117d441a18195 (reviewed 2026-09-29)
Core: 6/25 available; 17 partial; 2 missing

Required core blockers:
- business-dashboard [partial] (AKP-10): Saved layouts and saved reports exist. Summary, receivables, payables, cash, and tax widgets use posted-ledger reports; recent activity is operational. There is no expenses-by-category widget, and drill-down rows link to a document or the accounting page rather than the journal lines behind every total.
- products-and-services [partial] (AKP-07): Media and per-item multiple-tax behavior remain open.
- customers [partial] (AKP-08): Statements, immutable sharing, PDF and automatic reminders exist on web and Expo. Contact people, separate billing/shipping addresses, bulk customer import/export and authenticated portal remain open.
- sales-invoices [partial] (AKP-07): Cancel, restore, archive, duplicate, history, line discounts, multiple line taxes, attachments, and CSV import/export are implemented. Send and remind return 503 EMAIL_UNAVAILABLE unless a mail provider is configured. Recurrence is the recurring-activity capability.
- vendors-and-bills [partial] (AKP-01): The API covers vendor contacts and defaults, attachments, history, cancel/restore, split payments, and vendor CSV. Web page tests only cover the import-link permission. Recurring bills are the recurring-activity capability.
- payment-and-bank-accounts [partial] (AKP-02): Saved default payment accounts, exact movement summaries, statement review/resume and mobile CSV/FX workflows exist. Bank-account bulk state changes and broader performance acceptance remain open.
- transfers [partial] (AKP-02): Same-currency and reviewed-rate cross-currency transfers post equal and opposite reconciled legs. Expo selects an immutable exchangeRateId and the fresh local workflow verifies16NZD to10USD. Web cross-currency transfer acceptance remains separate. Transfers have no edit or void lifecycle.
- financial-reports [partial] (AKP-05): Server month/quarter columns, configurable NZ presets, exact cash-source recognition, CSV/PDF and Expo reporting exist. Category dimensions are unsupported; reports remain in company NZD base currency. Installed-device acceptance remains open.
- tax [partial] (AKP-11): GST registration settings, supported preparation boxes, immutable saved returns and external-filing records exist; the application does not submit to IRD. Invoice lines can carry multiple taxes. A reusable tax-rate catalogue and compound or withholding tax types remain open.
- currencies-and-localization [partial] (AKP-06): The organisation catalogue, immutable dated rates, locale, timezone and financial-year settings exist. Sources retain base-currency snapshots; reviewed foreign settlements and period-end revaluation post exact realized/unrealized differences with next-day reversal. Fresh web and Expo workflow evidence is in docs/evidence/feature-verification/2026-11-08. Reports remain NZD-only; broader currency-policy and native-device acceptance remain separate.
- company-settings [partial] (AKP-11): Business identity, invoice defaults and template appearance exist. Currency, locale and financial-year settings and automatic reminder schedules are implemented. Email templates and a persistent notification centre remain open; live mail delivery is separate.
- companies-and-organisations [partial] (AKP-03): Create, rename, switch, and ledger isolation are implemented and tested. Archive is implemented on POST /api/organisations/:id/archive and in the web and mobile company screens, but no automated test calls it. Restore and ownership transfer are not implemented.
- users-and-permissions [partial] (AKP-03): Fixed owner, admin, accountant, member, and read-only roles, hashed invitations, and server permission checks are implemented. Custom roles are not implemented, and invitations are share links rather than outbound email.
- customer-portal [missing] (AKP-08): Customers cannot authenticate, manage profiles, or list invoices, statements, payments, and receipts.
- attachments-and-uploads [partial] (AKP-07): Invoices, bills, bank transactions and reviewed expense receipts have scoped attachments. Receipt upload/read/delete has real role/tenant tests and web/Expo browser proof. Item/customer attachment parity and installed-device acceptance remain open.
- import-export [partial] (AKP-09): Items, invoices, vendors, bill export, and bank transactions have preview or import and export paths. Customers, accounts, journals, categories, and taxes do not.
- search-bulk-actions-notifications [partial] (AKP-12): Items support server bulk activate, deactivate, and delete. There is no organisation-scoped cross-domain search and no persistent notification centre.
- external-api-and-api-keys [missing] (AKP-13): No API-key lifecycle, scoped external API, OpenAPI publication, or webhook delivery exists.
- mobile-coverage [partial] (AKP-10): Expo includes full reporting, statements/reminders, mapped CSV/reconciliation, bank defaults/FX and recurring templates. Authenticated customer portal, installed-device/native release acceptance and broader parity remain open.

